IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nsw-duties-core`

-- Duties Act 1997 (New South Wales) -- the buyer's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the buyer -- of a home or of vacant residential land (including a first home buyer, a spouse taking a share of
-- the home, and a foreign person), and the applicant to register a motor vehicle. "What duty do I pay on this home or
-- land, and by when? Am I a first home owner, is my purchase eligible, and do I pay no duty? What must I do if I do not
-- move in? Is a transfer of the home to my spouse duty-free? Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty? What duty do I pay to
-- register this car?" Every question is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state, and is
-- answered by the rules in nsw-duties-core.l4; this module builds the core's records from plain answers and restates no
-- rule.
--
-- One case is one purchase (one dutiable transaction) by you, alone or with one other person, or one application to
-- register one vehicle. The same facts carry the same input names in every question, so a form can ask them once.
--
-- THE YEAR'S AMOUNTS. The s 32 table in the deposit holds the amounts for the year beginning 1 July 2019. For a later
-- year, enter the five threshold amounts and the premium threshold the Chief Commissioner publishes for that year under
-- s 33AF (not deposited); the base amounts are worked out from them under s 33AD. For a contract signed from 1 July 2019
-- to 30 June 2020 the Act's own amounts are used whatever is entered.
--
-- Edition: Duties Act 1997 No 123, corpus version 2025-01-01, Open Australian Legal Corpus as at 10 March 2025; NOT THE
-- CURRENT OFFICIAL TEXT AND IT MAY BE OUT OF DATE. BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Duties Act 1997 (NSW) -- the buyer's questions`

-- The year's adjustable amounts, from the six answers.
GIVEN `the year's range 2 threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the year's range 3 threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the year's range 4 threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the year's range 5 threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the year's range 6 threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the year's premium threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Adjustable amounts`
`the year's amounts from` MEANS
    `Adjustable amounts` OF `the year's range 2 threshold`, `the year's range 3 threshold`, `the year's range 4 threshold`,
                            `the year's range 5 threshold`, `the year's range 6 threshold`, `the year's premium threshold`

-- A buyer who is an individual, from the plain answers. The scheme's two ownership tests (s 71(2)(a)) are asked as one
-- answer and set in the first field; the second is then FALSE, which gives the same result. Fields a question does not
-- read are set from that question's answers or to FALSE, as each question's comment says.
GIVEN `owned or approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `with a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse owned or approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `years of age` IS A NUMBER
      `citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `foreign` IS A BOOLEAN
      `permanent resident or retirement visa holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ownership share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Purchaser
`an individual buyer` MEANS
    Purchaser WITH
        `kind` IS `an individual`
        `the s 73(2) trustee exception applies` IS FALSE
        `has owned residential property in Australia` IS `owned or approved`
        `has been a party to an approved application under the scheme` IS FALSE
        `has a spouse` IS `with a spouse`
        `the spouse has owned residential property in Australia` IS `spouse owned or approved`
        `the spouse has been a party to an approved application under the scheme` IS FALSE
        `age` IS `years of age`
        `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident` IS `citizen or permanent resident`
        `is an approved equity partner` IS FALSE
        `is a foreign person` IS `foreign`
        `is a permanent resident or a retirement visa holder` IS `permanent resident or retirement visa holder`
        `share` IS `ownership share`

-- The approved equity partner under an approved shared equity scheme (s 73A(2)): only its share is read.
GIVEN `ownership share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Purchaser
`the approved equity partner` MEANS
    Purchaser WITH
        `kind` IS `a company or a partnership`
        `the s 73(2) trustee exception applies` IS FALSE
        `has owned residential property in Australia` IS FALSE
        `has been a party to an approved application under the scheme` IS FALSE
        `has a spouse` IS FALSE
        `the spouse has owned residential property in Australia` IS FALSE
        `the spouse has been a party to an approved application under the scheme` IS FALSE
        `age` IS 0
        `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident` IS FALSE
        `is an approved equity partner` IS TRUE
        `is a foreign person` IS FALSE
        `is a permanent resident or a retirement visa holder` IS FALSE
        `share` IS `ownership share`

-- The purchase for the scheme questions (Part 8 Division 1), from the plain answers. The foreign-person facts are not read
-- by the scheme and are FALSE.
GIVEN `the day the contract was signed` IS A DATE
      `the price` IS A NUMBER
      `the value` IS A NUMBER
      `what is on the land` IS A `What is on the land`
      `I am buying the whole property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involves a business or business premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a holiday home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I intend to live in it as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am buying under an approved shared equity scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am buying with one other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my co-buyer has owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my co-buyer has a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my co-buyer's spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my co-buyer's age` IS A NUMBER
      `my co-buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my share` IS A NUMBER
      `my co-buyer's share` IS A NUMBER
      `we are buying as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Home purchase`
`the scheme purchase from` MEANS
    `Home purchase` WITH
        `the day of the agreement or transfer` IS `the day the contract was signed`
        `the consideration` IS `the price`
        `the unencumbered value` IS `the value`
        `the land` IS `what is on the land`
        `is for the whole of the property` IS `I am buying the whole property`
        `involves a business or business premises` IS `it involves a business or business premises`
        `is a holiday home` IS `it is a holiday home`
        `a first home owner intends to live in it as a principal place of residence` IS `I intend to live in it as my principal place of residence`
        `is under an approved shared equity scheme` IS `I am buying under an approved shared equity scheme`
        `the purchasers` IS append `the buyers` `the equity partner`
        `as joint tenants` IS `I am buying with one other person` AND `we are buying as joint tenants`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `an individual buyer` `I have owned residential property or had an approved application` `I have a spouse`
                       `my spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` `my age`
                       `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` FALSE FALSE `my share`
        `my co-buyer` MEANS `an individual buyer` `my co-buyer has owned residential property or had an approved application` `my co-buyer has a spouse`
                                `my co-buyer's spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` `my co-buyer's age`
                                `my co-buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` FALSE FALSE `my co-buyer's share`
        `the buyers` MEANS IF `I am buying with one other person` THEN LIST `me`, `my co-buyer` ELSE LIST `me`
        `the share left` MEANS 100 MINUS `my share` MINUS (IF `I am buying with one other person` THEN `my co-buyer's share` ELSE 0)
        `the equity partner` MEANS IF `I am buying under an approved shared equity scheme` THEN LIST (`the approved equity partner` `the share left`) ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Buying a home or land -- transfer duty (Chapter 2)`

@export What is the dutiable value of my purchase of a home or land (s 21)?
GIVEN `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in dollars, including any debt you take over (s 22)
      `the value` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property is worth on the open market, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance, in dollars (s 23)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the dutiable value of my purchase` IS
    `the dutiable value of the property` `the price` `the value`

@export What transfer duty do I, the buyer (the transferee, s 13), pay on this home or land, at the general or premium rate (ss 21, 32, 32A, 33AC-33AD)?
GIVEN `the day the contract was signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract (or, if there is no contract, the transfer) was first signed: liability for duty arises then (s 12)
      `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in dollars, including any debt you take over (s 22)
      `the value` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property is worth on the open market, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance, in dollars (s 23)
      `what is on the land` IS A `What is on the land` @desc What the property is: one house or one flat (a granny flat or one let room does not count); one house or flat and a shop; a building under construction that will be one house or flat; a strata lot used or fit to be used as a home; vacant land zoned residential; two or more dwellings; or other land
      `it is also used for non-residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the land is also used for purposes other than residential ones (s 32B)
      `the parcel is more than 2 hectares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parcel of land is larger than 2 hectares (s 32C)
      `the year's range 2 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc For the financial year (1 July to 30 June) in which you signed, the minimum threshold amount of threshold range 2 published by the Chief Commissioner under s 33AF ($14,000 in the Act; ignored for a contract signed between 1 July 2019 and 30 June 2020)
      `the year's range 3 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 3 ($30,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 4 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 4 ($81,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 5 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 5 ($304,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 6 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 6 ($1,013,000 in the Act)
      `the year's premium threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's premium rate threshold for residential land in s 32A ($3,040,000 in the Act)
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `What transfer duty do I pay on this home or land` IS
    `the transfer duty` `the day the contract was signed`
        (`the year's amounts from` `the year's range 2 threshold` `the year's range 3 threshold` `the year's range 4 threshold`
                                   `the year's range 5 threshold` `the year's range 6 threshold` `the year's premium threshold`)
        (`the dutiable value of the property` `the price` `the value`) `what is on the land`
        `it is also used for non-residential purposes` `the parcel is more than 2 hectares`

@export By what day must I lodge the contract (or a written statement) with my purchaser's declaration, and pay the transfer duty, to avoid a tax default (ss 15, 16, 16A, 17)?
GIVEN `the day the contract was signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract (or, if there is no contract, the transfer) was first signed: liability for duty arises then (s 12)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I lodge and pay the transfer duty` IS
    `the last day to lodge and pay` `the day the contract was signed`

@export What is an adjustable amount (a threshold) for a year, worked out from the Sydney CPI (s 33AC)?
GIVEN `the amount in the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount before any adjustment, in dollars: 14000, 30000, 81000, 304000, 1013000 (the s 32 thresholds) or 3040000 (the s 32A premium threshold)
      `A` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All Groups Index) for Sydney for the March quarter just before the financial year (s 33AB, s 33AC(2))
      `B` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All Groups Index) for Sydney for the March quarter of 2019
      `the amount for the previous year` IS A NUMBER @desc The same amount as it applied for the previous financial year, in dollars (s 33AC(4))
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the adjustable amount for the year` IS
    `the s 33AC adjusted amount` `the amount in the Act` `A` `B` `the amount for the previous year`

§§ `First home buyers -- the First Home Buyers Assistance Scheme (Part 8 Division 1)`

-- Situation: buying your first home or a vacant block to build it on.

@export Am I a first home owner for the First Home Buyers Assistance Scheme (s 71)?
GIVEN `I have owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever owned (alone or with anyone) land in Australia with a home on it, or a company title home, or been a party to an approved application under the scheme; do not count property you held only as a trustee or executor (s 71(6)); do count an ACT Commonwealth leasehold (s 71(8))
      `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are married or living together as a couple in a de facto relationship; leave out a husband or wife you have separated from with no intention of resuming, if the Chief Commissioner is satisfied of that (s 71(4), (5))
      `my spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse has ever owned land in Australia with a home on it (or a company title home), or been a party to an approved application under the scheme
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a first home owner` IF
    -- s 71 reads only the ownership and spouse answers; age 30, citizen, not foreign and a 100% share are placeholders.
    `the purchaser is a first home owner`
        (`an individual buyer` `I have owned residential property or had an approved application` `I have a spouse`
                               `my spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` 30 TRUE FALSE FALSE 100)

@export Is my purchase eligible under the First Home Buyers Assistance Scheme, and do I pay no duty (ss 70-76, 78A(1), 78B)?
GIVEN `the day the contract was signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract (or, if there is no contract, the transfer) was first signed: liability for duty arises then (s 12)
      `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in dollars, including any debt you take over (s 22)
      `the value` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property is worth on the open market, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance, in dollars (s 23)
      `what is on the land` IS A `What is on the land` @desc What the property is: one house or one flat (a granny flat or one let room does not count); one house or flat and a shop; a building under construction that will be one house or flat; a strata lot used or fit to be used as a home; vacant land zoned residential; two or more dwellings; or other land
      `I am buying the whole property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (with your co-buyer, if any) are buying the whole of the property, not a share of it (s 74(2))
      `it involves a business or business premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the purchase includes a business or business premises; a farm with a private dwelling on it does not count (s 75(1))
      `it is a holiday home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the property is a holiday home (s 75(2))
      `I intend to live in it as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or your co-buyer, as a first home owner) intend to move in within 12 months of completion and live there as your principal place of residence for at least 12 months; for vacant land, whether you intend to build your home on it (s 74(1), s 76, s 76A(1))
      `one of us is in the Permanent Forces and each of us is enrolled to vote in NSW` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day of the contract, you or your co-buyer is a member of the Permanent Forces of the Australian Defence Force and each of you is enrolled to vote in NSW State elections (s 76(6))
      `I am buying under an approved shared equity scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying under a shared equity scheme approved by the Chief Commissioner, with an approved equity partner holding the rest (s 73A(2), s 281)
      `I have owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever owned (alone or with anyone) land in Australia with a home on it, or a company title home, or been a party to an approved application under the scheme; do not count property you held only as a trustee or executor (s 71(6)); do count an ACT Commonwealth leasehold (s 71(8))
      `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are married or living together as a couple in a de facto relationship; leave out a husband or wife you have separated from with no intention of resuming, if the Chief Commissioner is satisfied of that (s 71(4), (5))
      `my spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse has ever owned land in Australia with a home on it (or a company title home), or been a party to an approved application under the scheme
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, the holder of a permanent visa, or a New Zealand citizen on a special category visa (Dictionary, s 73(5))
      `I am buying with one other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one other person is buying the property with you
      `my co-buyer has owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a co-buyer: whether they have ever owned land in Australia with a home on it, or been a party to an approved application under the scheme (otherwise FALSE)
      `my co-buyer has a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a co-buyer: whether they are married or in a de facto relationship (you, if you are their spouse) (otherwise FALSE)
      `my co-buyer's spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a co-buyer with a spouse: whether that spouse (you, if it is you) has ever owned residential property in Australia or had an approved application (otherwise FALSE)
      `my co-buyer's age` IS A NUMBER @desc If you have a co-buyer: their age in years (otherwise any number)
      `my co-buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a co-buyer: whether they are an Australian citizen or permanent resident (otherwise FALSE)
      `my share` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of the property, as a percentage (100 if you are buying alone; ignored for joint tenants, who hold equal shares, s 14)
      `my co-buyer's share` IS A NUMBER @desc Your co-buyer's share, as a percentage (0 if none)
      `we are buying as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your co-buyer are buying as joint tenants (FALSE if you are buying alone or as tenants in common)
GIVETH A `First home buyer answer`
DECIDE `Is my purchase eligible under the scheme, and do I pay no duty` IS
    `the first home buyer answer`
        (`the scheme purchase from` `the day the contract was signed` `the price` `the value` `what is on the land`
             `I am buying the whole property` `it involves a business or business premises` `it is a holiday home`
             `I intend to live in it as my principal place of residence` `I am buying under an approved shared equity scheme`
             `I have owned residential property or had an approved application` `I have a spouse`
             `my spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` `my age`
             `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `I am buying with one other person`
             `my co-buyer has owned residential property or had an approved application` `my co-buyer has a spouse`
             `my co-buyer's spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` `my co-buyer's age`
             `my co-buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `my share` `my co-buyer's share` `we are buying as joint tenants`)
        (`the residence requirement applies` `one of us is in the Permanent Forces and each of us is enrolled to vote in NSW` FALSE)

@export What transfer duty do I pay as a first home buyer: none under s 78A(1), or, if the purchase is not eligible, the general or premium rate?
GIVEN `the day the contract was signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract (or, if there is no contract, the transfer) was first signed: liability for duty arises then (s 12)
      `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in dollars, including any debt you take over (s 22)
      `the value` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property is worth on the open market, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance, in dollars (s 23)
      `what is on the land` IS A `What is on the land` @desc What the property is: one house or one flat (a granny flat or one let room does not count); one house or flat and a shop; a building under construction that will be one house or flat; a strata lot used or fit to be used as a home; vacant land zoned residential; two or more dwellings; or other land
      `I am buying the whole property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (with your co-buyer, if any) are buying the whole of the property, not a share of it (s 74(2))
      `it involves a business or business premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the purchase includes a business or business premises; a farm with a private dwelling on it does not count (s 75(1))
      `it is a holiday home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the property is a holiday home (s 75(2))
      `I intend to live in it as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or your co-buyer, as a first home owner) intend to move in within 12 months of completion and live there as your principal place of residence for at least 12 months; for vacant land, whether you intend to build your home on it (s 74(1), s 76, s 76A(1))
      `one of us is in the Permanent Forces and each of us is enrolled to vote in NSW` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day of the contract, you or your co-buyer is a member of the Permanent Forces of the Australian Defence Force and each of you is enrolled to vote in NSW State elections (s 76(6))
      `I am buying under an approved shared equity scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying under a shared equity scheme approved by the Chief Commissioner, with an approved equity partner holding the rest (s 73A(2), s 281)
      `I have owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever owned (alone or with anyone) land in Australia with a home on it, or a company title home, or been a party to an approved application under the scheme; do not count property you held only as a trustee or executor (s 71(6)); do count an ACT Commonwealth leasehold (s 71(8))
      `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are married or living together as a couple in a de facto relationship; leave out a husband or wife you have separated from with no intention of resuming, if the Chief Commissioner is satisfied of that (s 71(4), (5))
      `my spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse has ever owned land in Australia with a home on it (or a company title home), or been a party to an approved application under the scheme
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, the holder of a permanent visa, or a New Zealand citizen on a special category visa (Dictionary, s 73(5))
      `I am buying with one other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one other person is buying the property with you
      `my co-buyer has owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a co-buyer: whether they have ever owned land in Australia with a home on it, or been a party to an approved application under the scheme (otherwise FALSE)
      `my co-buyer has a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a co-buyer: whether they are married or in a de facto relationship (you, if you are their spouse) (otherwise FALSE)
      `my co-buyer's spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a co-buyer with a spouse: whether that spouse (you, if it is you) has ever owned residential property in Australia or had an approved application (otherwise FALSE)
      `my co-buyer's age` IS A NUMBER @desc If you have a co-buyer: their age in years (otherwise any number)
      `my co-buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a co-buyer: whether they are an Australian citizen or permanent resident (otherwise FALSE)
      `my share` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of the property, as a percentage (100 if you are buying alone; ignored for joint tenants, who hold equal shares, s 14)
      `my co-buyer's share` IS A NUMBER @desc Your co-buyer's share, as a percentage (0 if none)
      `we are buying as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your co-buyer are buying as joint tenants (FALSE if you are buying alone or as tenants in common)
      `it is also used for non-residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the land is also used for purposes other than residential ones (s 32B)
      `the parcel is more than 2 hectares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parcel of land is larger than 2 hectares (s 32C)
      `the year's range 2 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc For the financial year (1 July to 30 June) in which you signed, the minimum threshold amount of threshold range 2 published by the Chief Commissioner under s 33AF ($14,000 in the Act; ignored for a contract signed between 1 July 2019 and 30 June 2020)
      `the year's range 3 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 3 ($30,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 4 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 4 ($81,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 5 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 5 ($304,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 6 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 6 ($1,013,000 in the Act)
      `the year's premium threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's premium rate threshold for residential land in s 32A ($3,040,000 in the Act)
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `What transfer duty do I pay as a first home buyer` IS
    `the duty for a first home buyer`
        (`the scheme purchase from` `the day the contract was signed` `the price` `the value` `what is on the land`
             `I am buying the whole property` `it involves a business or business premises` `it is a holiday home`
             `I intend to live in it as my principal place of residence` `I am buying under an approved shared equity scheme`
             `I have owned residential property or had an approved application` `I have a spouse`
             `my spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` `my age`
             `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `I am buying with one other person`
             `my co-buyer has owned residential property or had an approved application` `my co-buyer has a spouse`
             `my co-buyer's spouse has owned residential property or had an approved application` `my co-buyer's age`
             `my co-buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `my share` `my co-buyer's share` `we are buying as joint tenants`)
        (`the residence requirement applies` `one of us is in the Permanent Forces and each of us is enrolled to vote in NSW` FALSE)
        (`the year's amounts from` `the year's range 2 threshold` `the year's range 3 threshold` `the year's range 4 threshold`
                                   `the year's range 5 threshold` `the year's range 6 threshold` `the year's premium threshold`)
        `it is also used for non-residential purposes` `the parcel is more than 2 hectares`

§§ `If I do not move in -- the residence requirement (ss 76, 76A)`

-- Situation: the Chief Commissioner approved your application under the scheme in advance, and you may not meet the
-- residence requirement.

@export Have I met the residence requirement of the First Home Buyers Assistance Scheme (s 76)?
GIVEN `one of us is in the Permanent Forces and each of us is enrolled to vote in NSW` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day of the contract, you or your co-buyer is a member of the Permanent Forces of the Australian Defence Force and each of you is enrolled to vote in NSW State elections (s 76(6))
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has exempted you from the residence requirement (s 76(2)(b))
      `I moved in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or another first home owner buying with you) moved in to live there as your principal place of residence
      `months from completion to moving in` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months after completion (when you became entitled to possession and the transfer was registered, s 76(5)) you moved in
      `months I lived there without a break` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months in a row you have lived there as your principal place of residence
      `months the Chief Commissioner allowed me to move in` IS A NUMBER @desc 12, or the longer period the Chief Commissioner approved for starting to live there (s 76(1))
      `months of living there the Chief Commissioner requires` IS A NUMBER @desc 12, or the shorter period the Chief Commissioner approved (s 76(2)(a))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the residence requirement` IF
    `the residence requirement is complied with`
        (`the residence requirement applies` `one of us is in the Permanent Forces and each of us is enrolled to vote in NSW` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement`)
        `I moved in` `months from completion to moving in` `months I lived there without a break`
        `months the Chief Commissioner allowed me to move in` `months of living there the Chief Commissioner requires`

@export If I do not meet the residence requirement, must I give the Chief Commissioner written notice and pay the relevant duty (s 76A(2))?
GIVEN `my application was approved in advance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your application in anticipation of your meeting the residence requirement (s 76A(1))
      `one of us is in the Permanent Forces and each of us is enrolled to vote in NSW` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day of the contract, you or your co-buyer is a member of the Permanent Forces of the Australian Defence Force and each of you is enrolled to vote in NSW State elections (s 76(6))
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has exempted you from the residence requirement (s 76(2)(b))
      `I moved in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or another first home owner buying with you) moved in to live there as your principal place of residence
      `months from completion to moving in` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months after completion (when you became entitled to possession and the transfer was registered, s 76(5)) you moved in
      `months I lived there without a break` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months in a row you have lived there as your principal place of residence
      `months the Chief Commissioner allowed me to move in` IS A NUMBER @desc 12, or the longer period the Chief Commissioner approved for starting to live there (s 76(1))
      `months of living there the Chief Commissioner requires` IS A NUMBER @desc 12, or the shorter period the Chief Commissioner approved (s 76(2)(a))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give notice and pay the relevant duty` IF
    `the s 76A(2) condition binds the applicant` `my application was approved in advance`
        (`the residence requirement is complied with`
             (`the residence requirement applies` `one of us is in the Permanent Forces and each of us is enrolled to vote in NSW` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement`)
             `I moved in` `months from completion to moving in` `months I lived there without a break`
             `months the Chief Commissioner allowed me to move in` `months of living there the Chief Commissioner requires`)

@export By what day must I give the Chief Commissioner written notice and pay the relevant duty, if I do not meet the residence requirement (s 76A(2))?
GIVEN `the day of completion` IS A DATE @desc The day of completion: when you became entitled to possession and the transfer to you was registered (s 76(5))
      `months the Chief Commissioner allowed me to move in` IS A NUMBER @desc 12, or the longer period the Chief Commissioner approved for starting to live there (s 76(1))
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I give notice and pay the relevant duty` IS
    `the last day to give notice and pay the relevant duty` `the day of completion` `months the Chief Commissioner allowed me to move in`

@export How much relevant duty must I pay if I do not meet the residence requirement (s 76A(3))?
GIVEN `the day the contract was signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract (or, if there is no contract, the transfer) was first signed: liability for duty arises then (s 12)
      `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in dollars, including any debt you take over (s 22)
      `the value` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property is worth on the open market, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance, in dollars (s 23)
      `what is on the land` IS A `What is on the land` @desc What the property is: one house or one flat (a granny flat or one let room does not count); one house or flat and a shop; a building under construction that will be one house or flat; a strata lot used or fit to be used as a home; vacant land zoned residential; two or more dwellings; or other land
      `it is also used for non-residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the land is also used for purposes other than residential ones (s 32B)
      `the parcel is more than 2 hectares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parcel of land is larger than 2 hectares (s 32C)
      `the year's range 2 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc For the financial year (1 July to 30 June) in which you signed, the minimum threshold amount of threshold range 2 published by the Chief Commissioner under s 33AF ($14,000 in the Act; ignored for a contract signed between 1 July 2019 and 30 June 2020)
      `the year's range 3 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 3 ($30,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 4 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 4 ($81,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 5 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 5 ($304,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 6 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 6 ($1,013,000 in the Act)
      `the year's premium threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's premium rate threshold for residential land in s 32A ($3,040,000 in the Act)
      `the duty I have paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much duty you have already paid on the purchase, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much relevant duty must I pay` IS
    `the relevant duty`
        (`the transfer duty` `the day the contract was signed`
             (`the year's amounts from` `the year's range 2 threshold` `the year's range 3 threshold` `the year's range 4 threshold`
                                        `the year's range 5 threshold` `the year's range 6 threshold` `the year's premium threshold`)
             (`the dutiable value of the property` `the price` `the value`) `what is on the land`
             `it is also used for non-residential purposes` `the parcel is more than 2 hectares`)
        `the duty I have paid`

§§ `Transferring the home to my spouse (Part 8 Division 4)`

-- Situation: you are transferring the home, or a share of it, to your husband, wife or de facto partner, or taking a share
-- from them.

@export Is the transfer of our home (or a share of it) between me and my spouse exempt from transfer duty (s 104B)?
GIVEN `what is on the land` IS A `What is on the land` @desc What the property is: one house or one flat (a granny flat or one let room does not count); one house or flat and a shop; a building under construction that will be one house or flat; a strata lot used or fit to be used as a home; vacant land zoned residential; two or more dwellings; or other land
      `we are` IS A `The couple` @desc Whether you are a married couple, de facto partners who have lived in the relationship for at least 2 years before the transfer, de facto partners for less than 2 years, or not a couple
      `afterwards we hold it as joint tenants or in equal shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the transfer, the two of you hold the property as joint tenants or as tenants in common in equal shares (s 104B(1)(a))
      `it is our home, or we will build our home on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is your principal place of residence when the transfer happens, or, for vacant land or a building under construction, you intend it to be the site of your principal place of residence (s 104B(1)(b))
      `it is used only as a home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is used solely for residential purposes; one room used for a business conducted mainly elsewhere does not count (s 104B(1)(c), (2))
      `only the two of us are parties to the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transferor and the transferee are only you and your spouse, with no one else a party (s 104B(1)(d))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the transfer to my spouse exempt` IF
    `the transfer is exempt under s 104B`
        (`Spouse transfer` OF `what is on the land`, `we are`, `afterwards we hold it as joint tenants or in equal shares`,
                              `it is our home, or we will build our home on it`, `it is used only as a home`,
                              `only the two of us are parties to the transfer`)

@export What transfer duty is payable on the transfer of our home (or a share of it) between me and my spouse (ss 104B, 104C)?
GIVEN `the day the transfer was signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the transfer (or the agreement for it) was first signed: liability for duty arises then (s 12)
      `the price for the share transferred` IS A NUMBER @desc What is paid for the share being transferred, in dollars, including any debt taken over (0 if nothing)
      `the value of the share transferred` IS A NUMBER @desc What the share being transferred is worth, ignoring any mortgage, in dollars
      `what is on the land` IS A `What is on the land` @desc What the property is: one house or one flat (a granny flat or one let room does not count); one house or flat and a shop; a building under construction that will be one house or flat; a strata lot used or fit to be used as a home; vacant land zoned residential; two or more dwellings; or other land
      `we are` IS A `The couple` @desc Whether you are a married couple, de facto partners who have lived in the relationship for at least 2 years before the transfer, de facto partners for less than 2 years, or not a couple
      `afterwards we hold it as joint tenants or in equal shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the transfer, the two of you hold the property as joint tenants or as tenants in common in equal shares (s 104B(1)(a))
      `it is our home, or we will build our home on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is your principal place of residence when the transfer happens, or, for vacant land or a building under construction, you intend it to be the site of your principal place of residence (s 104B(1)(b))
      `it is used only as a home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is used solely for residential purposes; one room used for a business conducted mainly elsewhere does not count (s 104B(1)(c), (2))
      `only the two of us are parties to the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transferor and the transferee are only you and your spouse, with no one else a party (s 104B(1)(d))
      `the non-residential apportionment factor` IS A NUMBER @desc If the land is also used for other purposes: the non-residential apportionment factor, as a fraction from 0 to 1, from the Register of Land Values or as the Chief Commissioner considers fair (s 104C(3)); otherwise 0
      `the parcel is more than 2 hectares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parcel of land is larger than 2 hectares (s 32C)
      `the year's range 2 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc For the financial year (1 July to 30 June) in which you signed, the minimum threshold amount of threshold range 2 published by the Chief Commissioner under s 33AF ($14,000 in the Act; ignored for a contract signed between 1 July 2019 and 30 June 2020)
      `the year's range 3 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 3 ($30,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 4 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 4 ($81,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 5 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 5 ($304,000 in the Act)
      `the year's range 6 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's minimum threshold amount of threshold range 6 ($1,013,000 in the Act)
      `the year's premium threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The same year's premium rate threshold for residential land in s 32A ($3,040,000 in the Act)
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `What transfer duty is payable on the transfer to my spouse` IS
    `the duty on a transfer between spouses`
        (`Spouse transfer` OF `what is on the land`, `we are`, `afterwards we hold it as joint tenants or in equal shares`,
                              `it is our home, or we will build our home on it`, `it is used only as a home`,
                              `only the two of us are parties to the transfer`)
        `the day the transfer was signed`
        (`the year's amounts from` `the year's range 2 threshold` `the year's range 3 threshold` `the year's range 4 threshold`
                                   `the year's range 5 threshold` `the year's range 6 threshold` `the year's premium threshold`)
        (`the dutiable value of the property` `the price for the share transferred` `the value of the share transferred`)
        `the non-residential apportionment factor`
        (NOT `it is used only as a home`)
        `the parcel is more than 2 hectares`

§§ `Foreign persons -- surcharge purchaser duty (Chapter 2A)`

-- Situation: you, or the person buying with you, are a foreign person.

@export Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty on this home or land, and how much (ss 104J, 104R, 104U)?
GIVEN `the day the contract was signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract (or, if there is no contract, the transfer) was first signed: liability for duty arises then (s 12, s 104Q)
      `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in dollars, including any debt you take over (s 22)
      `the value` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property is worth on the open market, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance, in dollars (s 23)
      `what is on the land` IS A `What is on the land` @desc What the property is: one house or one flat (a granny flat or one let room does not count); one house or flat and a shop; a building under construction that will be one house or flat; a strata lot used or fit to be used as a home; vacant land zoned residential; two or more dwellings; or other land
      `it is used for primary production` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is exempt from land tax as land used for primary production (Dictionary, s 104I)
      `it is also used for non-residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the land is also used for purposes other than residential ones (s 104ZB)
      `I am a foreign person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a foreign person under the Foreign Acquisitions and Takeovers Act 1975 (Cth) as s 104J modifies it: an Australian citizen never is; a New Zealand citizen on a special category visa is treated as not limited in time; otherwise, broadly, someone not ordinarily resident in Australia
      `I am a permanent resident or retirement visa holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a permanent visa, or a Subclass 405 or 410 retirement visa (s 104ZKA, s 104ZKB)
      `I am buying with one other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one other person is buying the property with you
      `my co-buyer is a foreign person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a co-buyer: whether they are a foreign person, in the same sense (otherwise FALSE)
      `my co-buyer is a permanent resident or retirement visa holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have a co-buyer: whether they hold a permanent visa or a retirement visa (otherwise FALSE)
      `my share` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of the property, as a percentage (100 if you are buying alone; ignored for joint tenants, who hold equal shares, s 14)
      `my co-buyer's share` IS A NUMBER @desc Your co-buyer's share, as a percentage (0 if none)
      `we are buying as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your co-buyer are buying as joint tenants (FALSE if you are buying alone or as tenants in common)
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `Do I owe surcharge purchaser duty, and how much` IS
    `the surcharge purchaser duty the transferee is liable for` `me`
        `the day the contract was signed` (`the dutiable value of the property` `the price` `the value`)
        `what is on the land` `it is used for primary production` `it is also used for non-residential purposes`
        `the buyers` (`I am buying with one other person` AND `we are buying as joint tenants`)
    WHERE
        -- The scheme's facts are not read for surcharge purchaser duty: they are fixed (no ownership, citizen or permanent
        -- resident TRUE, age 30), and only the foreign-person facts and shares count.
        `me` MEANS `an individual buyer` FALSE FALSE FALSE 30 TRUE `I am a foreign person` `I am a permanent resident or retirement visa holder` `my share`
        `my co-buyer` MEANS `an individual buyer` FALSE FALSE FALSE 30 TRUE `my co-buyer is a foreign person` `my co-buyer is a permanent resident or retirement visa holder` `my co-buyer's share`
        `the buyers` MEANS IF `I am buying with one other person` THEN LIST `me`, `my co-buyer` ELSE LIST `me`

@export By what day must I pay surcharge purchaser duty to avoid a tax default (s 104W)?
GIVEN `the day the contract was signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract (or, if there is no contract, the transfer) was first signed: liability for duty arises then (s 12, s 104Q)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I pay surcharge purchaser duty` IS
    `the last day to lodge and pay` `the day the contract was signed`

§§ `Registering a car -- motor vehicle registration duty (Chapter 9)`

@export Is my application to register this vehicle (or transfer its registration to me) charged with duty (s 261)?
GIVEN `it has been registered in NSW before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has been registered under the Road Transport Act 2013 before
      `it will be registered in the same name as before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is to be registered in the same name or names as it was last registered in
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application charged with duty` IF
    `the application is charged with duty under s 261` `it has been registered in NSW before` `it will be registered in the same name as before`

@export What is the dutiable value of the vehicle (s 266)?
GIVEN `the price of the vehicle` IS A NUMBER @desc What you gave for the vehicle, in money or money's worth, in dollars
      `the market value of the vehicle` IS A NUMBER @desc What the vehicle is worth on the market when it is registered, in dollars
      `GST on a car for use by a disabled person` IS A NUMBER @desc If the supply of the car to you is GST-free under Subdivision 38-P of the GST Act (cars for use by disabled people): the GST included in the figures above, in dollars; otherwise 0
      `an extended warranty premium in the price` IS A NUMBER @desc Any premium for extended warranty insurance included in the figures above, in dollars; otherwise 0
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the dutiable value of the vehicle` IS
    `the dutiable value of the vehicle` `the price of the vehicle` `the market value of the vehicle` `GST on a car for use by a disabled person` `an extended warranty premium in the price`

@export Am I exempt from registration duty on this vehicle (s 267(1), (6)-(7B), s 268)?
GIVEN `I am entitled to it because the registered owner died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are beneficially entitled to the vehicle following the death of the person in whose name it was registered in NSW (s 267(1))
      `it is a relationship breakdown transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registration is being transferred between you and your former husband, wife, de facto partner or domestic partner because the marriage or relationship has ended or broken down, as matrimonial or relationship property, under a binding financial agreement, a court order or a property division agreement (for a domestic relationship, a court order under the Property (Relationships) Act 1984), as the Chief Commissioner is satisfied (s 267(6), (6A), (7))
      `my Veterans' Entitlements Act pension` IS A `Veterans' Entitlements Act pension` @desc The disability pension you are eligible for under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986: none or under 70% of the general rate; 70% or more of the general rate (s 22(3)); the extreme disablement adjustment rate (s 22(4)); the intermediate rate (s 23); or the special rate (s 24)
      `my MRCA impairment points` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are a member or former member under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004: the impairment points assessed under that Act (otherwise 0)
      `I receive or have received MRCA compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible for, receive, or have ever received compensation or a special rate disability pension under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004
      `it is to be registered conditionally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is to be registered conditionally under the Road Transport Act 2013 rules (s 267(7B))
      `I registered it in another state or territory and paid duty there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is or was registered by you in another Australian state or territory and duty was paid there on that registration (s 268)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I exempt from registration duty` IF
    `the application is exempt under s 267 or s 268`
        (`Vehicle exemption facts` OF `I am entitled to it because the registered owner died`, `it is a relationship breakdown transfer`,
                                      `my Veterans' Entitlements Act pension`, `my MRCA impairment points`, `I receive or have received MRCA compensation`,
                                      `it is to be registered conditionally`, `I registered it in another state or territory and paid duty there`)

@export What duty do I pay to register this vehicle (ss 261, 265, 266, 267, 268)?
GIVEN `it has been registered in NSW before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has been registered under the Road Transport Act 2013 before
      `it will be registered in the same name as before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is to be registered in the same name or names as it was last registered in
      `the kind of vehicle` IS A `Kind of vehicle` @desc What kind of vehicle it is: one built mainly to carry 9 or fewer people (a sedan, station wagon, coupe, convertible, 4WD or panel van with seats and windows, three wheel car, small bus, motor home or snow vehicle); a motor cycle; a bus seating more than 9; a hearse or invalid conveyance; or another vehicle
      `the price of the vehicle` IS A NUMBER @desc What you gave for the vehicle, in money or money's worth, in dollars
      `the market value of the vehicle` IS A NUMBER @desc What the vehicle is worth on the market when it is registered, in dollars
      `GST on a car for use by a disabled person` IS A NUMBER @desc If the supply of the car to you is GST-free under Subdivision 38-P of the GST Act (cars for use by disabled people): the GST included in the figures above, in dollars; otherwise 0
      `an extended warranty premium in the price` IS A NUMBER @desc Any premium for extended warranty insurance included in the figures above, in dollars; otherwise 0
      `I am entitled to it because the registered owner died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are beneficially entitled to the vehicle following the death of the person in whose name it was registered in NSW (s 267(1))
      `it is a relationship breakdown transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registration is being transferred between you and your former husband, wife, de facto partner or domestic partner because the marriage or relationship has ended or broken down, as matrimonial or relationship property, under a binding financial agreement, a court order or a property division agreement (for a domestic relationship, a court order under the Property (Relationships) Act 1984), as the Chief Commissioner is satisfied (s 267(6), (6A), (7))
      `my Veterans' Entitlements Act pension` IS A `Veterans' Entitlements Act pension` @desc The disability pension you are eligible for under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986: none or under 70% of the general rate; 70% or more of the general rate (s 22(3)); the extreme disablement adjustment rate (s 22(4)); the intermediate rate (s 23); or the special rate (s 24)
      `my MRCA impairment points` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are a member or former member under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004: the impairment points assessed under that Act (otherwise 0)
      `I receive or have received MRCA compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible for, receive, or have ever received compensation or a special rate disability pension under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004
      `it is to be registered conditionally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is to be registered conditionally under the Road Transport Act 2013 rules (s 267(7B))
      `I registered it in another state or territory and paid duty there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is or was registered by you in another Australian state or territory and duty was paid there on that registration (s 268)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What duty do I pay to register this vehicle` IS
    `the motor vehicle registration duty`
        (`the application is charged with duty under s 261` `it has been registered in NSW before` `it will be registered in the same name as before`)
        (`Vehicle exemption facts` OF `I am entitled to it because the registered owner died`, `it is a relationship breakdown transfer`,
                                      `my Veterans' Entitlements Act pension`, `my MRCA impairment points`, `I receive or have received MRCA compensation`,
                                      `it is to be registered conditionally`, `I registered it in another state or territory and paid duty there`)
        (`the dutiable value of the vehicle` `the price of the vehicle` `the market value of the vehicle` `GST on a car for use by a disabled person` `an extended warranty premium in the price`)
        `the kind of vehicle`

@export Must I lodge a statement of the vehicle's dutiable value with my application to register it (s 262)?
GIVEN `it has been registered in NSW before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has been registered under the Road Transport Act 2013 before
      `it will be registered in the same name as before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is to be registered in the same name or names as it was last registered in
      `I am entitled to it because the registered owner died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are beneficially entitled to the vehicle following the death of the person in whose name it was registered in NSW (s 267(1))
      `it is a relationship breakdown transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registration is being transferred between you and your former husband, wife, de facto partner or domestic partner because the marriage or relationship has ended or broken down, as matrimonial or relationship property, under a binding financial agreement, a court order or a property division agreement (for a domestic relationship, a court order under the Property (Relationships) Act 1984), as the Chief Commissioner is satisfied (s 267(6), (6A), (7))
      `my Veterans' Entitlements Act pension` IS A `Veterans' Entitlements Act pension` @desc The disability pension you are eligible for under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986: none or under 70% of the general rate; 70% or more of the general rate (s 22(3)); the extreme disablement adjustment rate (s 22(4)); the intermediate rate (s 23); or the special rate (s 24)
      `my MRCA impairment points` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are a member or former member under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004: the impairment points assessed under that Act (otherwise 0)
      `I receive or have received MRCA compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible for, receive, or have ever received compensation or a special rate disability pension under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004
      `it is to be registered conditionally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is to be registered conditionally under the Road Transport Act 2013 rules (s 267(7B))
      `I registered it in another state or territory and paid duty there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is or was registered by you in another Australian state or territory and duty was paid there on that registration (s 268)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I lodge a statement of the dutiable value` IF
    `the application is chargeable with duty under Chapter 9`
        (`the application is charged with duty under s 261` `it has been registered in NSW before` `it will be registered in the same name as before`)
        (`Vehicle exemption facts` OF `I am entitled to it because the registered owner died`, `it is a relationship breakdown transfer`,
                                      `my Veterans' Entitlements Act pension`, `my MRCA impairment points`, `I receive or have received MRCA compensation`,
                                      `it is to be registered conditionally`, `I registered it in another state or territory and paid duty there`)
